1. expr rescue fallback
   Integer("abc") rescue 0  -> 0
   Integer("42") rescue 0   -> 42
2. it catches StandardError only
   (raise NotImplementedError) rescue 0 -> propagated NotImplementedError
3. how it binds
   value = raise("boom") rescue "fallback"  -> value is "fallback"
   as a bare argument, p(expr rescue 0):   SyntaxError
   with its own parentheses, p((expr rescue 0)): compiles
4. a rescue clause in a def needs no begin
   parse("q") -> "method-level rescue"
5. a rescue clause inside do...end works; inside { } it is a syntax error
   do |x| ... rescue => e ... end   compiles
   { |x| ... rescue => e ... }      SyntaxError
   rescued inside do...end: "inside a do block (1)"
6. the modifier form is fine inside { }
   modifier inside braces (1)
7. Integer() raises where to_i does not
   "abc".to_i                    -> 0
   "12abc".to_i                  -> 12
   Integer("abc")                -> ArgumentError: invalid value for Integer(): "abc"
   Integer("abc", exception: false) -> nil
8. the trap: the modifier hides every StandardError, including a typo
   nil.upcse rescue "default" -> "default" (the NoMethodError from the typo is gone)
